.TH LINECAST 1 "September 2026" "linecast 2.6.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
linecast \- weather, tides, the sun, the moon, and maps drawn for the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B linecast
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.I COMMAND
[\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B linecast
is a terminal weather and celestial observation suite. It brings weather
forecasts, radar animations, solar arcs, lunar phases with multiple cultural
calendars, night sky views, tide tables, and street or terrain maps directly
into terminal emulators using Braille characters, Unicode block glyphs, and
24-bit true color.
.PP
On Linux, linecast runs on pure Python using standard library facilities,
requiring no external C or Python dependencies.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B weather
Conditions now, the day's temperature curve, the forecast, and alerts.
.TP
.B sunshine
The sun's arc across the sky, dawn to dusk, or the whole year.
.TP
.B moon
The moon as it looks tonight, its rise and set, and a month calendar.
.TP
.B sky
The stars, planets, and Milky Way over you, as you would see them.
.TP
.B tides
Tide chart from the nearest station, or a global model where there is none.
.TP
.B radar
Weather radar over a map, the last hour and the next.
.TP
.B maps
Street maps, hillshaded terrain, and routes.
.SH SETTINGS COMMANDS
.TP
.B location [\fIshow\fR | \fIset\fR \fIPLACE\fR | \fIauto\fR | \fIsearch\fR \fIQUERY\fR]
A fixed place, instead of the one your IP address suggests.
.TP
.B language [\fIshow\fR | \fICODE\fR | \fIauto\fR]
Language code: en, fr, es, de, it, pt, nl, pl, no, sv, is, da, fi, ja, ko, zh, th, id, uk, or vi.
.TP
.B units [\fIshow\fR | \fImetric\fR | \fIimperial\fR]
Units configuration.
.TP
.B clock [\fIshow\fR | \fI12h\fR | \fI24h\fR]
Clock time format.
.TP
.B week [\fIshow\fR | \fImonday\fR | \fIsunday\fR | \fIsaturday\fR]
The day the moon calendar's week opens on.
.TP
.B icons [\fIshow\fR | \fInerd\fR | \fIemoji\fR | \fIplain\fR]
Icon style for rendering.
.TP
.B calendar [\fIshow\fR | \fICALENDAR\fR]
Calendar system: chinese, japanese, korean, vietnamese, thai, hawaiian, samoan, chamorro, refaluwasch, islamic, hebrew, almanac, or none.
.TP
.B culture [\fIshow\fR | \fICULTURE\fR]
Whose constellations the sky draws: IAU (none) or various cultural sky traditions.
.SH HOUSEKEEPING COMMANDS
.TP
.B link
Make short commands (weather, moon, sunshine, tides, radar, maps, sky) beside linecast via symlinks or shell aliases.
.TP
.B doctor
Check configuration, file locations, terminal capabilities, and provider status.
.TP
.B completion [\fIbash\fR | \fIzsh\fR | \fIfish\fR | \fInu\fR]
Emit shell completion script.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show program version and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-location " PLACE"
Override location for one run (name or coordinates, e.g. "41.88,-87.63").
.TP
.BI \-\-lang " CODE"
Override language for one run.
.TP
.BR \-\-metric ", " \-\-imperial
Override units for one run.
.TP
.BR \-\-12h ", " \-\-24h
Override time format for one run.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/linecast/config.json
User configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/linecast/
Cache directory for offline tiles, astronomical catalogues, and data.
.SH SEE ALSO
Further documentation and upstream source code are available at
https://github.com/ashuttl/linecast and https://github.com/Leimsoto/linecast-for-debian.
